## 2. Root-Cause Fix: 404 on /api/posture/latest

### Symptom

Every page load showed a 404 in the Network tab:

```
GET http://localhost:3000/api/posture/latest
404 Not Found
{"message": "No detections yet"}
```

### Cause

The route existed but had **no authentication middleware**:

```js
app.get("/api/posture/latest", getLatest);
//                              ↑ no authenticateJWT here
```

Inside `getLatest`, the controller does:

```js
const detection = await getLatestDetection(
    req.user?.userId || req.query.user_id,
    req.query.session_id || null
);
```

Without `authenticateJWT`, `req.user` is always `undefined`. The frontend also sends no `user_id` query param. So the call resolves to:

```js
getLatestDetection(undefined, null)
```

Which runs the SQL:

```sql
WHERE user_id = $1   -- $1 = undefined → NULL
```

PostgreSQL returns zero rows. The controller then correctly returns:

```json
HTTP 404
{"message": "No detections yet"}
```

This happens **every time, even when data exists**, because the query can never find rows for `user_id = NULL`.

### Fix

```js
// src/app.js
app.get(
  "/api/posture/latest",
  authenticateJWT,   // ← added
  getLatest
);

app.get(
  "/api/posture/stream",
  authenticateJWT,   // ← added
  streamPosture
);
```

`/api/frame` is intentionally left public — `camera.py` posts to it without a browser session.

### Secondary fix

`EventSource` does not support custom headers, so it cannot send a Bearer token. It does send cookies on same-origin requests automatically. For development servers running on a different port (e.g. VS Code Live Server on `:5500` pointing at Express on `:3000`), the cookie is cross-origin and may not be forwarded. `LiveCoach.js` now fetches the user first and passes `?user_id=` as a query parameter as a fallback — the backend already handles `req.query.user_id` as a fallback when `req.user` is absent.

