## 6. Known Limitations & Next Steps

### What still needs work (from the review)

#### History pagination should move to the backend
Currently fetches 200 rows and filters client-side. This works for a prototype but will break at scale. Future: pass `?status=`, `?startDate=`, `?endDate=`, `?page=` directly to `GET /api/history`.

#### AI Insight is rule-based, not Ollama
The Dashboard and Analytics "AI Insight" sections generate descriptive text from analytics numbers using JavaScript string templates. This is clearly labelled in the code. To replace with real Ollama output, add a `GET /api/insights/latest` endpoint that reads from `ai_recommendations`.

#### Live Coach does not capture a browser webcam
The camera area shows SSE posture data but does not call `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia()`. The intended architecture uses `camera.py` as the video source, not the browser. If browser-based capture is wanted later, a separate webcam capture module would be needed that mirrors the `camera.py` POST flow from JavaScript.

#### Analytics uses approximate weekly grouping
The monthly chart groups 28 days into 4 buckets of 7 by array index, not by calendar week. This can mis-align if the trend data doesn't start on a Monday.

#### Error display
`api.js` logs errors to the console but does not surface them in the UI. A toast/notification component should be added so users see "Could not reach server" rather than a silent empty state.

### How to run the complete system

```bash
# Terminal 1 — Database (Docker)
docker-compose up -d

# Terminal 2 — MediaPipe service
cd src/camera
uvicorn pose_service:app --reload --port 5001

# Terminal 3 — Node backend (serves the frontend too)
npm start                     # → http://localhost:3000

# Terminal 4 — Camera sender (needs a registered user first)
export CAMERA_USER_ID=<uuid>
export BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/frame
python src/camera/camera.py

# Browser
open http://localhost:3000/auth/SignIn.html
```

Open the browser at `http://localhost:3000` (not Live Server) so that cookies are same-origin and the SSE stream works without the `?user_id=` fallback.
